in @prism

in @optics
in @glass
in @nl
in @mirror/lens
in @mirror/lens/cli

# @mirror/lens/cli/bootstrap — the autopoietic phase machine as a stage.
#
# Fourth of eight verb sub-stages forward-promised in
# docs/specs/cli-as-prism.md §3 (table at §3 + §3.1 shape sketch).
# Drives the 7 phases of self-hosting (per docs/specs/bootstrap.md —
# the autopoietic ladder) through the standard five-op surface.
#
# === The bootstrap.split strain — sequence vs branch ===
#
# Per cli-as-prism §4.3: bootstrap STRAINS on split. The 7 phases of
# self-hosting SEQUENCE; they don't BRANCH. So `mirror bootstrap
# split` has no obvious meaning. The spec settles on "enumerate
# sub-phase dependencies" — weak but defensible. The constraint is
# honest about graph algebra being its native habitat; bootstrap is a
# phase machine (linear with dependencies), and the fit gets looser.
#
# §4.3's finding: when the underlying manifold isn't graph-shaped,
# `split` strains because `split` IS the graph-walk verb. Worth
# naming explicitly: this stage exists as a `stage` at the CLI
# altitude because the dispatcher's five-op surface is what users
# learn once; the sub-altitude resolution (whether the engine that
# actually walks phases is more sequence-shaped than stage-shaped)
# can land later. The CLI surface is the stage; the engine the stage
# drives is the autopoietic ladder.
#
# === Note: no mirror.spec command yet ===
#
# Unlike compile, kintsugi, and shatter, bootstrap does NOT yet have
# a `command bootstrap { ... }` declaration in mirror.spec — the
# self-hosting phase machine is consumed by the bootstrap/ Rust crate
# directly (per docs/specs/bootstrap.md's seven-phase ladder), not yet
# lifted into the mirror.spec cli block. This stage shard is the CLI
# surface forward-promised by cli-as-prism.md §2.1; the mirror.spec-
# side declaration is a subsequent tick (forward-promise: when
# bootstrap is no longer the Rust ladder and IS the substrate stage,
# mirror.spec gains its command block and this shard's actions wire
# to it).
#
# === Family placement ===
#
# Parent bench: @mirror/lens/cli (shards/mirror/lens/cli.mirror).
# Family root:  @mirror/lens    (shards/mirror/lens.mirror).
# Sibling stages:
#   @mirror/lens/cli/compile    — landed at 737330f
#   @mirror/lens/cli/kintsugi   — landed previously this tick
#   @mirror/lens/cli/shatter    — landed previously this tick
#   @mirror/lens/cli/join       — peer-entry (Glanville's verb)
#   @mirror/lens/cli/reflect    — VSM System 5 view
#   @mirror/lens/cli/time       — Elm-style time travel
#   @mirror/lens/cli/crack      — third-state lifecycle
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/mirror/lens/cli/bootstrap.mirror` declares
# `@mirror/lens/cli/bootstrap` and only that.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/cli-as-prism.md §3, §3.1 (shape sketch),
#               §2.1 (bootstrap sub-stage decision),
#               §4.3 (THE strain — split on a phase machine),
#               §7 (default-op rule: bootstrap declares `default
#               focus` — bootstrap.settle advances a phase, a real
#               side effect on substrate state; the user wants to
#               see status before advancing),
#               docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §1.2 (stage),
#               docs/specs/bootstrap.md (the seven-phase autopoietic
#               ladder this stage's settle advances).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]
#                      (stage IS a sub-prism specialization),
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]]
#                      (file path matches namespace),
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] (shift =
#                      basis transformation; here, shift between
#                      phase representations — eigenvalue, line count,
#                      proof).
# Related shards: lens/cli.mirror (parent bench),
#                 lens/cli/compile.mirror (sibling — the build
#                 stage; bootstrap drives the substrate IN, compile
#                 drives the substrate OUT),
#                 glass.mirror (imperfect / transparency carriers).

stage @mirror/lens/cli/bootstrap {
  # Per cli-as-prism §7: bootstrap declares `default focus` — reads
  # are free; advancing a phase is a real substrate-state side effect
  # the user wants to see status (`focus`) before triggering. Bare
  # `mirror bootstrap` reports phase status (no write); explicit
  # `settle` advances. Only compile and shatter declare `default
  # settle` (artifact-write acts that don't escalate); bootstrap's
  # settle escalates into the autopoietic ladder, so the default must
  # read.
  default focus

  # The five operations the produced prism exposes on the bootstrap
  # sub-manifold (the autopoietic phase machine's state). Each
  # operand below names the natural shape of the manifold's element
  # at that op's slot, per the spec §3.1 sketch convention and
  # §2.1's per-verb decisions:
  #   focus    phase        — report phase status (no write)
  #   project  predicate    — filter to one phase (or phases matching
  #                          a predicate, e.g. "all phases that
  #                          consume @kintsugi")
  #   split    candidate    — enumerate sub-phase dependencies
  #                          (§4.3: this op STRAINS; the manifold is
  #                          linear-with-dependencies, not graph-
  #                          shaped; enumerating sub-phase deps is
  #                          the spec's chosen reading; the fit is
  #                          weak but defensible)
  #   shift    basis        — shift between phase representations:
  #                          eigenvalue / line count / proof
  #                          (same content, different basis;
  #                          [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]])
  #   settle   phase        — the ONE write; advance one phase;
  #                          emits proof block recording the
  #                          autopoietic transition (which Rust
  #                          shrinks; which substrate primitive
  #                          lifts to replace it)
  focus    phase
  project  predicate
  split    candidate
  shift    basis
  settle   phase
}

# === Bootstrap-specific actions ===
#
# No mirror.spec `command bootstrap { ... }` declaration yet (see
# the "no mirror.spec command yet" note above). The CLI surface
# action signature lands here as the substrate forward-promise; the
# Rust runtime walks this declaration when the bootstrap engine lifts
# into substrate. Substrate-pull discipline per
# [[architecture-fragmentation-is-the-rust-substrate]].
#
# Honest `partials` from birth (per recognition #306): the return
# type is the substrate's `imperfect` functor (declared in
# shards/glass.mirror as `imperfect(a, e, l) = success(a) |
# partial(a, l) | failure(e, l)`). A phase advance that fully
# discharges its obligations returns success; a phase advance that
# lifts loss (e.g. a sub-phase dependency that did not converge but
# the phase advances under accept-loss semantics, like the `\!`
# fracture mode) returns partial-with-loss carrying the
# transparency-tagged residual opacity. The autopoietic ladder's
# proof-block carries the same shape: each phase's settle records
# what shrank and what remains imperfect.

# bootstrap() — advance one phase of the autopoietic ladder against
# the current substrate state. Returns the imperfect carrying the
# advanced-phase ref on success, the partial carrying the
# transparency-tagged residual loss on tolerable sub-phase shortfall,
# the failure with reason on hard error.
bootstrap() -> imperfect { \ }

# bootstrap_phase(phase) — same as bootstrap but with an explicit
# phase pin. The dispatcher walks to that phase and runs its settle;
# useful for replay or for partial-bootstrap workflows where the
# user wants to advance a specific phase rather than the next one.
bootstrap_phase(phase: ref) -> imperfect { \ }

out @mirror/lens/cli/bootstrap
out bootstrap
out bootstrap_phase
